{"status":"question","question":{"text":"Before I can name a stack or a first slice, I need the one-liner: in plain language, what is this thing and who's it for? (I hear the add-ons — dark mode, a Chrome extension, email digests, and \"all of those features\" — and I'm capturing every one of them, but I'm deliberately NOT planning them now. This first mission builds only the foundation: a skeleton that boots, a real test runner a human can watch run, and one thin slice proving they're wired together. Every feature you name gets recorded in the vision doc and becomes its own mission the moment the foundation lands. So: what's the core product, in a sentence or two?)","recommended":"Give me the core idea in your own words — e.g. \"a tool that ingests X and shows me Y\" — and I'll handle the rest."},"prd":"# Mission: (title pending Align)\n\n**Type:** feature\n**Goal:** Establish the project foundation — a booting skeleton, a runnable test system, and one thin vertical slice proving they are connected.\n\n_(PRD in progress — capturing the core product idea before recommending a stack and first slice. Named features are being recorded for deferral, not planned.)_\n\n## Deferred features (for the vision doc, not this mission)\n- Dark mode toggle\n- Chrome extension\n- Email digests\n- \"All of those features\" — pending the captain's core product description"}

